PLAN: {"customer_persona": "Everyday compact-SUV buyers comparing engine and gearbox choices, passenger and luggage space, useful equipment and ownership costs. Their actual route, household, location, budget and preferred trim remain unknown unless they choose to share them.", "decision_frame": "The strongest fit is the engine and trim whose gearbox, seating and equipment match what you need, and the thing still to verify is that exact version\u2019s current on-road quote.", "takeaway": "Choose an offered engine-and-gearbox combination, then confirm the equipment and current quote for its exact trim.", "primary_outcome": "Identify an offered CRETA engine, gearbox and trim combination to check against the buyer\u2019s needs.", "supporting_outcomes": ["Understand how the supported seating and cabin functions fit possible use.", "Separate confirmed equipment from the price, policy and measured evidence still needed."], "concerns": [{"topic": "powertrain", "why": "Manual and automatic availability changes with both engine and trim, even where trim names are similar.", "fact_ids": ["F003", "F005", "F006", "F008", "F009", "F065", "F066", "F067", "F068"]}, {"topic": "space-and-practicality", "why": "Split-seat flexibility does not establish personal passenger, luggage or parking fit.", "fact_ids": ["F001", "F022", "F023", "F063"]}, {"topic": "safety", "why": "Standard airbags and selected-trim driving assistance establish equipment, not a crash-test score.", "fact_ids": ["F025", "F031", "F032", "F034"]}, {"topic": "ownership", "why": "The dated conflicting entry amount is not a current local on-road quote and extended petrol warranty costs extra.", "fact_ids": ["F054", "F055", "F056", "F057", "F058"]}, {"topic": "running-costs", "why": "Measured fuel use, service costs and resale evidence are not supplied.", "fact_ids": []}], "usps": [{"id": "choose-your-gears", "name": "Pick the way you change gears", "fact_ids": ["F003", "F005", "F006", "F008", "F009", "F065", "F066", "F067", "F068"], "stop_id": "powertrain"}, {"id": "space-for-changing-plans", "name": "Space you can change with your plans", "fact_ids": ["F022", "F023"], "stop_id": "space-and-practicality"}, {"id": "airbags-from-the-start", "name": "Airbags from the very first trim", "fact_ids": ["F025"], "stop_id": "safety"}], "segments": [{"id": "opening", "title": "The button that holds the car still", "role": "intro", "goal": "MOMENT \u2014 Begin with the CRETA\u2019s supported stationary brake-holding function, then place it in a possible traffic stop without another greeting. SPOKEN / DEEPER \u2014 One 29-word alternative Browse opening uses F015/F016 for auto hold holding the stationary car without the brake staying pressed, standard from King, with automatic-only S(O), S(O) Knight and SX Premium feature rows and the actual engine-matrix exceptions kept deeper. VISUAL / HANDOFF \u2014 Use only the AUTO HOLD button im_pdf_e1266b7974b364c1c1ba, then hand off the engine-and-gearbox choice introduced by the three USPs, with an empty checkin.", "outcome": "", "topic": "powertrain", "fact_ids": ["F015", "F016"], "usp_ids": [], "visual_refs": ["im_pdf_e1266b7974b364c1c1ba"], "priority_topic": false, "stop_id": null, "fundamental": false, "word_budget": 29}, {"id": "three-anchors", "title": "The gearbox, rear seats and airbags", "role": "outcome", "goal": "MOMENT \u2014 Give exactly three memorable anchors and say the buyer can steer the tour without asking another question. SPOKEN / DEEPER \u2014 One 33-word alternative-opening batch names the unchanged Coach USPs using F003/F005/F006/F008/F009/F065\u2013F068, F022/F023 and F025, retaining that gearbox choice depends on engine and trim and turbo is automatic-only. VISUAL / HANDOFF \u2014 In this required three-USP opening only, change from manual lever im_pdf_3aa2ebf1c9ed94570455 to folded rear seats im_pdf_adb415f161dfc9567dde to airbags im_pdf_a54e8e56f4b50c2f5596, then hand off the non-turbo petrol engine as the first guided subject, with an empty checkin.", "outcome": "Choose which buying detail to explore", "topic": "highlights", "fact_ids": ["F003", "F005", "F006", "F008", "F009", "F065", "F066", "F067", "F068", "F022", "F023", "F025"], "usp_ids": ["choose-your-gears", "space-for-changing-plans", "airbags-from-the-start"], "visual_refs": ["im_pdf_3aa2ebf1c9ed94570455", "im_pdf_adb415f161dfc9567dde", "im_pdf_a54e8e56f4b50c2f5596"], "priority_topic": false, "stop_id": null, "fundamental": false, "word_budget": 33}, {"id": "engine-choices", "title": "The petrol, diesel and turbo engines", "role": "proof", "goal": "MOMENT \u2014 B1 notices the ordinary petrol engine and considers gearbox preference, B2 considers the diesel alternative, and B3 opens on the separate turbo engine as an engine-and-trim decision. SPOKEN / DEEPER \u2014 Reserve F015/F016 for the separate 23-word Explore overview only; assign B1 31 words to F003/F009/F065/F066 for ordinary petrol manual or automatic by trim, using SX manual-only and SX Premium offering both as concrete supported examples, B2 32 words to F003/F008/F067/F068 for diesel with SX Premium manual-only and the exact automatic set EX(O), S(O), King, King Knight and Lounge Edition, and B3 31 words to F003/F005/F006 for automatic-only turbo listed solely on King without making every King a turbo, keeping full matrix sets, complete technical quantities, F013/F014 and manufacturer descriptions F002/F010\u2013F012 deeper. VISUAL / HANDOFF \u2014 Give B1 only the petrol engine im_pdf_98cd4a320f9dbfd33bbd, B2 only the diesel engine im_pdf_5cd207807990f4eea283 and B3 only the turbo engine im_pdf_87bac17ee980151549ba, treating gearbox pairings as sourced selection information rather than visible mechanisms, handing off diesel, turbo and wheel/tyre choice respectively across 94 words with empty checkins.", "outcome": "Choose an engine and offered gearbox", "topic": "powertrain", "fact_ids": ["F002", "F003", "F004", "F005", "F006", "F007", "F008", "F009", "F010", "F