oom price and a current itemised dealer quote, keeping F054\u2019s 19 September 2026 \u20b910,90,700 entry amount and conflicting \u20b910.79 lakh structured value together deeper and reserving F057/F058 for establish. VISUAL / HANDOFF \u2014 Use only whole-car side view im_pdf_689090f045758facf9e2 as explicitly contextual imagery for this quote subject because no literal price document exists, then hand off the front-armrest compartment as the remaining equipment detail, with an empty checkin.", "outcome": "Get a current itemised on-road quote", "topic": "ownership", "fact_ids": ["F054", "F055", "F056", "F057", "F058"], "usp_ids": [], "visual_refs": ["im_pdf_689090f045758facf9e2"], "priority_topic": true, "stop_id": "ownership", "fundamental": false, "word_budget": 30}, {"id": "small-storage", "title": "The compartment beside the front seat", "role": "features", "goal": "MOMENT \u2014 Notice the open armrest compartment as a place for everyday small items without asserting a particular object\u2019s fit. SPOKEN / DEEPER \u2014 One 27-word batch uses F061 for standard front-armrest storage and sliding adjustment from King, retaining the continuous King/King Knight/Lounge Edition scope and adding no cooling, locking or capacity benefit. VISUAL / HANDOFF \u2014 Hold only the open compartment im_pdf_06658fba292467f801c7 for the entire batch, treating sliding as sourced function rather than an illustrated motion, then hand off the engine/trim and written warranty terms, counting this as space-and-practicality\u2019s second batch with an empty checkin.", "outcome": "Locate standard storage and sliding adjustment", "topic": "space-and-practicality", "fact_ids": ["F061"], "usp_ids": [], "visual_refs": ["im_pdf_06658fba292467f801c7"], "priority_topic": false, "stop_id": null, "fundamental": false, "word_budget": 27}, {"id": "terms", "title": "The terms and evidence still to confirm", "role": "establish", "goal": "MOMENT \u2014 Keep engine and trim together while moving from